---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — I Quit... Again!" description="The story behind I Quit... Again! and Dale Sackrider's health and fitness journey.">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">
        About I Quit... Again!
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mt-2">
        A candid journal about health, weight loss, running, discipline, and starting over as many times as it takes.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 space-y-6 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Welcome to <strong>I Quit... Again!</strong> This site began in 2008 as a personal, unfiltered online journal by <strong>Dale Sackrider</strong> to document the real, day-to-day struggle with weight loss, food discipline, and health.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        “Why call it 'I Quit... Again!'? Because like so many people on a health journey, I have started, made great progress, stumbled, quit, and had to find the discipline to start again.”
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        Over more than a decade, this site recorded hundreds of entries: from training for half-marathons and tracking daily calories to confronting adult-onset type 2 diabetes, testing diets, celebrating weight milestones, and learning how to navigate setbacks.
      </p>

      <h3>The Authors & Contributors</h3>
      <p>
        While primarily written by Dale Sackrider, friends and family members—including <strong>Albert Tubbs</strong>, <strong>Stephanie Sackrider</strong>, and <strong>Jason Fisher</strong>—contributed challenges, guest posts, and encouragement along the way.
      </p>

      <h3>Connecting</h3>
      <p>
        For leadership, cloud architecture, and professional writings, visit Dale's primary blog at <a href="https://dalesackrider.com">DaleSackrider.com</a>, and for family updates, check out <a href="https://sackrider.org">Sackrider.org</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
